sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph faithfully reproduces Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952), Schnakenberg (1979) and Murray (1981) supply the instability, the kinetics and the coat-marking wavelength idea. | oca2 and mc1r, not a measured 666 nm mode, account for cavefish pigment loss (Protas et al. 2006; Gross et al. 2009; McCauley, Hixon and Jeffery 2004). | Yamamoto, Stock and Jeffery (2004) and Yoshizawa et al. (2010) are the sources for eye degeneration and neuromast expansion. Neither is a Turing-wavelength result.; reconstructed_in_script: Metres per pixel are set so the fastest linear mode equals 6.656e-7 m. That length is the loop card, not a cavefish measurement. | Pass 2 adds a six-point diffusion-ratio sweep, an equal-diffusivity ablation, and a flank-versus-patch KS statistic. Pearson r, RMSE and the 660.7 nm nonlinear peak are unchanged from pass 1.; transfer_boundary: The GIF still composites a subcellular patch onto a whole-body photograph. High computer-vision similarity is dominated by the shared silhouette. It does not show that the camera resolved 666 nm.; does_not_claim: Does not claim optic-cup degeneration or neuromast expansion are produced by k_c. | Does not claim Schnakenberg parameters were identified in Astyanax tissue. | Does not claim a fossil predecessor. The chronoseries is the single extant cave morph at 0 Ma. The 24 µm sibling is a scale comparison, ratio 36.33.]; phenomenon_size: 484 nm (4.836e-07 m, log10=-6.316 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 484 nm to 1.1 mm): 484 nm:astyanax-mexicanus-bioelectric-polarity, 1.5 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-vertex-packing, 24 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength, 48 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-clock-wavefront, 109 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-morphogen-condensation, 133 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-elastic-buckling, 151 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-flux-canalization, 212 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.07.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02864>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng1700>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1525-142x.2004.04026.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-genet-102108-134216>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1000326> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

